# (Not the LOD logic: docs/rdp_exact.md rule 9.) 2-cycle, no TEX_LOD, a trilinear combiner ((TEXEL1 - TEXEL0) * LOD_FRACTION +
# TEXEL0, then COMBINED) on a texture of a level count of 0, whose next tile (tile 1, blue) was set apart: the oracle computes
# the LOD fraction because the combiner reads it, all ones for a level count of 0, so its pixels are TEXEL1, tile 1's blue; the
# console shows TEXEL0, the primitive's own tile (tile 0: the 4-texel ramp, red, black, black, green), as the model's fraction,
# 0 without TEX_LOD, gives. (A game draws a figure with such a combiner and never sets tile 1.)
rdram zero
